# LoveStream environment configuration
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values you need.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cross-network video calls (WebRTC TURN relay)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# STUN (bundled by default) is enough for calls on the same network and for
# many home networks, but calls between peers behind symmetric NATs / CGNAT
# (mobile hotspots, some ISPs) need a TURN relay to carry the media.
#
# Provide one or more TURN URLs (comma separated), plus credentials:
#
#   VITE_TURN_URLS=turn:your-turn-host:3478,turns:your-turn-host:443?transport=tcp
#   VITE_TURN_USERNAME=your-turn-username
#   VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=your-turn-credential
#
# Free options:
#   - Open Relay by Metered: sign up at https://www.metered.ca/tools/openrelay/
#     (free 20 GB/month), then use the REST API or dashboard credentials.
#   - Self-hosted coturn: https://github.com/coturn/coturn
#
# If unset, the app falls back to STUN-only. Direct connections still work,
# but symmetric-NAT pairs will fail and the call UI will show
# "CONNECTION FAILED" with a retry button instead of hanging forever.
# VITE_TURN_URLS=
# VITE_TURN_USERNAME=
# VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=
